  "result": "I stopped without an OK. The last verdict is `WITNESS_FAIL` on blind, and I've reported the node as defective: the `blind` scenario it plans can't be built.\n\n**Why blind can't work:**\n- The plan masks `rel.bearing` and expects unknown. But masking only drops a *measured* bearing; Core recomputes it from v's position and heading.\n- The only way to stop that is to leave out v's heading. Admission then rejects the trace, because the rule needs v's occupancy of c observed, which needs v's footprint, which needs the heading.\n- So no admissible trace makes the bearing alone undecided. My suggested fix for the plan is to mask `kin.speed` in blind. Core reads it straight from the speed field and never recomputes it, and the conflict check uses velocity, so it stays decided.\n\n**Rule:**\n- **Applicability:** the subject is moving, and its latest entry into or exit from a controlled-access region c was more than 0 s and at most `p.merge_window` ago.\n- **Obligation:** for every such c (same selection repeated), every other moving vehicle on c that has the subject ahead of it must not be in contact with the subject or in a traffic conflict with it.\n\nI added no narrowings of my own.\n\n**Witnesses:**\n- forbid, permit, idle and branch_1 are built and each judges a window after the entry. They appear to pass, but the gate only seems to report the first failure, so I haven't seen the adequacy check run.\n- The blind trace is set back to the forbid geometry so the file builds; the gate will report it as violated.\n\n**Gate runs:** I used four of the six.\n1. My mistake: I ran the gate command with a pipe attached, against the \"exactly this command\" rule. It ran on the untouched skeletons and probably counted against the budget.\n2. `CHECK_FAIL`: wrong component name on the bearing. I switched to the \"ahead\" form of the bearing atom, which is exactly \"longitudinal component positive\".\n3. `WITNESS_FAIL`: blind came back violated, not unknown.\n4. `WITNESS_FAIL`: my attempt to hide v's heading was rejected by admission.\n\nOne open risk: the node claims `kin.time`, and I use it only through the time-since-entry operator, with no explicit clock read. The gate never got as far as checking claims, so I don't know if it accepts that.\n\n`task_result.md` has the full record of the runs, choices and defect.",
